{"id":"n-20261014-o34zqo","category":"finance","display_title":"Ayalon Eyes Cal Acquisition","display_title_he":"איילון בוחנת רכישת כאל","short_summary":"Following the collapse of the Union-Harel transaction, insurance company Ayalon is exploring the acquisition of credit card firm Cal.","english_level":"C1","words":626,"reading_time":4,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Globes","domain":"globes.co.il","url":"https://www.globes.co.il/news/article.aspx?did=1001559423","title":"עסקת כאל: איילון בוחנת רכישה בשל הערכה שסיכוייה מול הרגולטור משופרים","published_at":"2026-10-13T15:41:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-13T15:41:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-14T06:13:30.770Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The Israeli financial landscape is currently witnessing renewed activity surrounding the credit card company Cal. Following the collapse of a four-billion-shekel acquisition deal by the Union-Harel consortium last month, the transaction is not definitively dead, but prospective buyers have begun to emerge. Among these interested parties is Ayalon Insurance, an organization controlled by Wobi (Wisr Globaltech) with fifty-nine percent ownership and led by CEO Sharon Reich. Ayalon has already held preliminary exploratory talks with Discount Bank, managed by Avi Levy, to examine the feasibility of such a purchase.","Discount Bank currently holds a seventy-two percent stake in Cal and is legally mandated by the Strum Law to divest its entire holdings by April 2027. According to market analysts, Ayalon operates as a relatively small player within the domestic insurance sector. Because of its modest market footprint, company management believes that regulatory approval from the Competition Authority might prove more attainable than it was for Union-Harel. However, uncertainties remain, particularly given that Wobi is simultaneously engaged in the complex process of acquiring the Altshuler Shaham investment house. Although Ayalon is technically a separate corporate entity, evaluating how the Competition Authority will view this dual involvement remains difficult. Conversely, some market participants argue that Ayalon's small market share could actually be presented as an opportunity to foster greater competition through the acquisition of Cal.","The original transaction involving Union—importer of Toyota vehicles and holder of a significant stake in Super-Pharm—and Harel fell apart due to stringent regulatory demands. The Competition Authority insisted that Union relinquish its retail holdings in Super-Pharm because Cal issues credit cards for Shufersal, which owns the Be drugstore chain, the second-largest pharmacy network in Israel. Although industry experts suggest a theoretical possibility that the original consortium might restructure the deal to appease regulators by bringing in additional business entities to dilute Union's shares, the probability is considered extremely low. Furthermore, the strict legal deadline of April 2027 places immense pressure on the process, whereas an alternative public stock offering is regarded as nearly impossible because the minority shareholder in Cal, the First International Bank of Israel, would look upon it unfavorably.","Meanwhile, Discount Bank has hinted at receiving various expressions of interest from both local and international parties during the past week. Historically, major insurance companies have actively attempted to acquire credit card issuers. The first to succeed was Clal Insurance, which acquired Max, the smallest of the credit card firms. Previously, Harel attempted to purchase Isracart, but that deal was de facto vetoed by the Competition Authority due to suspicions regarding data leakage from Cal in the health insurance domain, where Harel holds market dominance. Menora Mivtachim subsequently attempted to acquire Isracart and nearly succeeded, before Delek Group abruptly snatched it in the final stretch.","Financial observers note that Cal's market valuation may have significantly declined since the failed Union-Harel agreement. A massive blow occurred when Cal lost the lucrative El Al frequent flyer club contract, known as FlyCard, to its competitor Isracart. Although Cal, managed by Yafit Griani, subsequently introduced an alternative travel card named FlyAll to put up its own fight, the loss of this major asset has likely diminished its valuation, meaning future buyers may demand a lower purchase price.","Credit card companies remain highly attractive assets for insurance firms due to the reliable, non-seasonal nature of their revenues. Consumer spending on plastic transactions exhibits steady patterns throughout the year, with predictable peaks around the Passover and Tishrei holidays, supplemented by profitable foreign exchange commissions when travelers fly abroad or purchase from international e-commerce websites. As the formal expiration of the Union-Harel agreement approaches in November, the market continues to monitor whether Ayalon or other prospective buyers will formalize their interest in acquiring the financial institution before the final deadline."],"facts":[{"fact":"The 4 billion shekel deal to sell Cal to Union-Harel collapsed last month.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Ayalon Insurance is evaluating a potential acquisition of Cal, believing its smaller market share improves regulatory approval chances compared to Union-Harel.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Discount Bank holds 72% of Cal shares and is legally required to sell them by April 2027 under the Strum Law.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Ayalon is controlled by Wobi (59%) and managed by Sharon Reich.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The original Union-Harel deal collapsed because the Competition Authority demanded Union sell its holdings in Super-Pharm due to a conflict with Cal issuing a credit card for Shufersal, which owns the rival Be chain.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Cal recently lost the lucrative FlyCard agreement with El Al to Isracart, introducing a new card called FlyAll instead.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Israeli","lemma":"Israeli","pos":"adjective","he":"ישראלי","name":"false"},{"text":"financial","lemma":"financial","pos":"adjective","he":"פיננסי","name":false},{"text":"landscape","lemma":"landscape","pos":"noun","he":"נוף, בזירה","name":false},{"text":"is currently witnessing","lemma":"currently witness","pos":"verb","he":"חווה כעת","name":false},{"text":"renewed","lemma":"renewed","pos":"adjective","he":"מחודש","name":false},{"text":"activity","lemma":"activity","pos":"noun","he":"פעילות","name":false},{"text":"surrounding","lemma":"surrounding","pos":"preposition","he":"סביב","name":false},{"text":"credit card company","lemma":"credit card company","pos":"noun","he":"חברת כרטיסי אשראי","name":false},{"text":"Cal","lemma":"Cal","pos":"proper noun","he":"כאל","name":"true"},{"text":"Following","lemma":"following","pos":"preposition","he":"בעקבות","name":"false"},{"text":"collapse","lemma":"collapse","pos":"noun","he":"קריסה","name":false},{"text":"four-billion-shekel","lemma":"four-billion-shekel","pos":"adjective","he":"בסך ארבעה מיליארד שקל","name":false},{"text":"acquisition","lemma":"acquisition","pos":"noun","he":"רכישה","name":false},{"text":"deal","lemma":"deal","pos":"noun","he":"עסקה","name":false},{"text":"Union-Harel","lemma":"Union-Harel","pos":"proper noun","he":"יוניון-הראל","name":"true"},{"text":"consortium","lemma":"consortium","pos":"noun","he":"קונסורציום","name":false},{"text":"last month","lemma":"last month","pos":"noun phrase","he":"חודש שעבר","name":false},{"text":"transaction","lemma":"transaction","pos":"noun","he":"עסקה","name":false},{"text":"definitively","lemma":"definitively","pos":"adverb","he":"באופן סופי","name":false},{"text":"dead","lemma":"dead","pos":"adjective","he":"מת","name":false},{"text":"prospective","lemma":"prospective","pos":"adjective","he":"פוטנציאלי, מתעניין","name":false},{"text":"b